{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sports and Leisure", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "After the Fall", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Non-Defining Relative Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Relative clauses</span> are used to connect two separate clauses into a single sentence. They are also used to add information. <span class=\"strong\">Non-defining relative clauses</span> provide more information about a noun. However, this information is not needed to understand which noun is being talking about.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Non-defining relative clauses</span> can relate to the subject or object. For this kind of clause, the relative pronoun must be used. You cannot use <span class=\"italic\">that</span> in a <span class=\"strong\">non-defining relative clause</span>, but always <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for an object and <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for a person.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Non-defining relative clauses</span> can be placed after the subject of the sentence.</br> Example: </br><span class=\"italic\">Danielle, <span class=\"strong\">who was an expert climber</span>, broke both her legs in a climbing accident. </br>The hospital, <span class=\"strong\">which specializes in mountaineering injuries</span>, was two hours away by helicopter. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Non-defining relative clauses</span> are placed after the object. </br>Example: </br><span class=\"italic\">The doctors spoke with Danielle, <span class=\"strong\">who looked to be in a lot of pain</span>. </br>The doctors thought it was an amazing recovery, <span class=\"strong\">which is extremely rare with this type of injury</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Danielle, who had always had an tenacious spirit, was determined to walk again.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I now have to pay more attention and put less weight on my left foot, which is permanently weaker.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Several years ago, Danielle, who is an expert climber, survived a fall from one of the tallest mountain peaks in Alaska.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She spent over a year in the local hospital, which specializes in mountaineering injuries, and then several months in a wheelchair.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adverbial Clause of Place", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "An <span class=\"strong\">adverbial clause</span> is a group of words which have the same function as an adverb. Like all clauses, an <span class=\"strong\">adverbial clause</span> has a subject and a verb.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbial clauses </span>of place are used to express where something happens. An adverb of place often starts with a preposition like <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">in</span></span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">on</span> </span>or <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">near</span></span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use a <span class=\"strong\">subordinating conjunction </span>like <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">anywhere</span></span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">everywhere</span></span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">where</span> </span> or <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">wherever</span></span> to introduce the adverbial clause. </br>Example:</br><span class=\"italic\">Danielle tries to climb a mountain wherever she travels to. She is willing to travel anywhere mountains can be found.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In a world where there is so much pessimism, she never once lost her positive outlook.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Everywhere she goes, people ask her how she manages to do it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She is willing to go anywhere good climbing can be found. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She is back on the mountain and enters competitions wherever she travels.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "persistence", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the act of continuing to put forth an effort", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Danielle claims her success is due to dedication and persistence. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about adventurous activities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to scale", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to climb", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She was scaling a steep cliff with two other enthusiasts.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "enthusiast", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who is very interested in a particular subject", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The climbing enthusiasts met every week to practice. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "grip", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to hold something very tightly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She lost her grip and fell.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tenacious", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unwilling to accept defeat; persistent ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Danielle, who had always had a tenacious spirit, was determined to walk again.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to fulfil", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to complete something that was planned or expected", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Today, Danielle is fulfilling her dream.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dedication", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the ability to give a lot of time and energy to something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Danielle claims her success is due to dedication and persistence. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research adventurous moments in history.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create sentences in the past tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use relative clauses. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my work with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Research ten adventurous accomplishments.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a sentence to describe each one (i.e. Neil Armstrong walked on the moon.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Insert some extra information into each one by adding a relative clause (e.g. Neil Armstrong, who was from the United States, walked on the moon).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your ten sentences to a partner. ", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about sports and leisure time.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express complex statements using words like <span class=\"italic\">who</span>, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> or <span class=\"italic\">which</span>. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about where something is done. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Have you ever had an accident or injury when doing a sport? What happened?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Which adventurous activities have you tried? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Let's meet an adventurous character!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "type":