s": []}], "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le02ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le02ob07re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn10le02ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn10le02ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "Several years ago, Danielle, who is an expert climber, survived a fall from one of the tallest mountain peaks in Alaska. She had been scaling a steep cliff with two other enthusiasts when she lost her grip and fell. She was told at the time that her injuries, which were quite severe, might prevent her from ever walking again. She had broken her hip bone and had only limited movement in her left foot.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn10le02ob07re2img02.jpg", "text": "Danielle, who had always had a tenacious spirit, was determined to walk again. She spent over a year in the local hospital, which specializes in mountaineering injuries, and then several months in a wheelchair. In a world where there is so much pessimism, she never once lost her positive outlook. Her recovery was slow, but one and a half years after the accident, Danielle was able to stand on her feet and walk. The doctors thought it was a remarkable recovery. But for Danielle, walking was not enough. She dreamed of climbing again.", "time": "26000", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn10le02ob07re2img03.jpg", "text": "Today, Danielle is fulfilling her dream. She is back on the mountain and enters competitions wherever she travels, and she is willing to go anywhere good climbing can be found.\n</br>\nEverywhere she goes, people ask her how she manages to do it. Danielle claims her success is due to dedication and persistence. She says, \"I never gave up. I exercise as often as I can and always look for opportunities to climb. I've also had to learn to climb differently. I now have to pay more attention and put less weight on my left foot, which is permanently weaker. All in all, I have become a better climber as a result of the accident!\"", "time": "60000", "id": 3}]}}], "id": 1}], "type": "scholar", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "type": "sena"}